 "differences": [
  "The paper analyses 19 healthy, 17 post-surgery and 18 post-chemoradiation participants after exclusions; the deposit has 19 surgery and 19 chemoradiation recordings and does not say which were excluded, so none is flagged (subject_excluded_by_authors is False for all).",
  "Healthy folder 'Observer 1' has 21 files with IDs H01-H11, H17-H25 and H024; H024 holds exactly the same corrected arrays as H24 and is coded as the same person. In Chemoradiation, R19's corrected arrays (markers3D_corr and markers3D_corr_JAW) are identical to R16's and have R16's length (3647 frames) while R19's raw tracks have 2081 frames, so they look like a copy of R16's; the corrected channels of R19 are left empty here and its raw channels are kept.",
  "The paper reports repeatability SD of about 3.5 mm without and 2.5 mm with jaw compensation for range; the left-right range from the five repeated recordings computed here from the authors' arrays and frame labels is about 4.2 mm and 3.4 mm, so that value is not reproduced exactly (the authors' own range definition is not given in the deposit)."
 ],
